      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, it's clear and professional. But to be honest, looking at the \"Luxury Index\" score it just generated for that draft... it's actually pretty low. The tool is flagging it as \"standard\" rather than \"ultra-luxury\" because the adjective density is too sparse.\n\nI really don't want you to go overboard and just list synonyms, but we need this to feel much more high-end to attract the right clients. Can you try another version that really leans into that sense of exclusivity and grandeur? Aim for a much higher density of those prestige terms, but please—keep the 8,500 sq ft and the bedroom/bathroom specs in there so it's still a valid listing. Just make it feel significantly more \"expensive.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
